From 19dea59ae4b0f425ee25581b4f04e7227a8bfdde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:51:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] drm_hwcomposer: fix inverted test in CleanFailedCommit

CommitFrame() returns std::optional<AtomicCommitResult>, which is truthy
on SUCCESS. Testing it directly logged 'Failed to clean-up active
composition' on every frame where the clean-up WORKED, and logged nothing
when it genuinely failed.

That matters more than a stray log line: CleanFailedCommit() is the
commit that DISABLES EVERY PLANE while the CRTC stays ACTIVE, i.e. one
solid black frame on a lit panel, so this is the only record of how often
the screen is being blacked out -- and it read backwards.

Change-Id: I3ee1ddc2f0fa37a308b21dc27803ab5f096f2886
---
 drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
index 99d646f..a462f97 100644
--- a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
+++ b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
@@ -90,7 +90,13 @@ void DrmAtomicStateManager::CleanFailedCommit() {
   // signal the release fences from that composition to avoid hanging.
   AtomicCommitArgs cl_args{};
   cl_args.composition = std::make_shared<LayerToPlaneJoiningPlan>();
-  if (CommitFrame(cl_args, /* test_only */ false)) {
+  // CommitFrame() returns std::optional<AtomicCommitResult>, which is TRUTHY
+  // ON SUCCESS and nullopt on failure. Testing it directly inverted this: the
+  // error was logged on every frame where the clean-up WORKED, and nothing was
+  // logged when it genuinely failed. That matters more here than it looks --
+  // this is the commit that blanks the panel, so this line is the only record
+  // of how often the screen is being blacked out, and it read backwards.
+  if (!CommitFrame(cl_args, /* test_only */ false)) {
     ALOGE("Failed to clean-up active composition for pipeline %s",
           pipe_->connector->Get()->GetName().c_str());
   }
